<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Thank you again!<br><br>Is the Windows 11 problem only for the 1701, because I believe I used it for the RD-5R? But I did that 10 months ago.<br><br>My default 2024 M4 Mac Mini runs Windows 11 in Parallels virtualization, but I have access to Windows 10 and XP in Parallels on my older Intel Mac.  <br><br>Michael, W7ML</div></blockquote>The driver problem with newer radio. In the CPS menu radio type, you will see two group of radio the first one are radios that use MK22 CPU (GD77, RD-5R, 1801) the second group are the radios that use STM32 CPU. This newer radio type share the same STM32 in DFU mode driver.<br><br>BTW: the driver is here <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/drivers/" class="postlink">downloads/drivers/</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Mon Jan 06, 2025 11:55 pm</p><hr />
